<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.17.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01176</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.17.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>aa661f85-4ad2-4799-9945-c177d4121b4a</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="4cbb9077-36a0-41da-a973-346270ec3474" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q1-->
  <exercise data-content-id="4346f584-c163-4d4f-af5b-ff3f4e32e6dc" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(c(n)=c(n-1)+6\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(a(n)=7\\cdot a(n-1)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(b(n)=\\frac12b(n-1)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(c(n)=c(n-1)+6\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(d(n)=d(n-1)+20\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>For questions 1 – 3, match each sequence with one of the definitions. Note that only the part of the definition showing the relationship between the current term and the previous term is given so as not to give away the solutions.</para>
      <para>6, 12, 18, 24</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(c(n)=c(n-1)+6\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.17.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="f0bb4279-bc18-410e-9f1e-cf2a4f7c4a18" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(a{(\mathrm n})=7\cdot a(n-1)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(a{(\\mathrm n})=7\\cdot a(n-1)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(b(n)=\\frac12b(n-1)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(c(n)=c(n-1)+6\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(d(n)=d(n-1)+20\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>2, 14, 98, 686</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(a(n)=7\cdot a(n-1)\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.17.2.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q3-->
  <exercise data-content-id="9e8f3213-c781-466f-b0c9-960969c82d9e" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(b(n)=\frac12b(n-1)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(a{(\\mathrm n})=7\\cdot a(n-1)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(b(n)=\\frac12b(n-1)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(c(n)=c(n-1)+6\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(d(n)=d(n-1)+20\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>160, 80, 40, 20</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(b(n)=\frac{1}{2}b(n-1)\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.17.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q4-->
  <exercise data-content-id="3a1ca587-2e2c-4c2b-9366-97eff10d778b" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="7, 4, 1, -2, -5, arithmetic" data-solution-options="[&quot;7, 4, 1, -2, -5, geometric&quot;, &quot;7, -21, 63, -189, geometric&quot;, &quot;7, -21, 63, -189, arithmetic&quot;, &quot;7, 4, 1, -2, -5, arithmetic&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>For questions 4 – 5, select the first five terms of each sequence. Determine whether each sequence is arithmetic, geometric, or neither.</para>
      <para>\(a(1)=7\), \(a(n)=a(n−1)−3\) for \(n≥2\).</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 7, 4, 1, –2, –5, arithmetic</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.17.2.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q5-->
  <exercise data-content-id="a3ae435e-517b-4dd8-a419-01290f5af8d7" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="3, 30, 300, 3000, 30000, geometric" data-solution-options="[&quot;3, 30, 300, 3000, 30000, arithmetic&quot;, &quot;3, 30, 300, 3000, 30000, geometric&quot;, &quot;3, 13, 23, 33, 43, geometric&quot;, &quot;3, 13, 23, 33, 43, arithmetic&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(c(1)=3\), \(c(n)=10⋅c(n−1)\) for \(n≥2\).</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 3, 30, 300, 3000, 30000, geometric</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.17.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q6-->
  <exercise data-content-id="50bf737d-9ce3-4460-aee2-daf2767eecf9" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(c(n)=5 \cdot c(n-1)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(a(n)=\\frac{1}{3} \\cdot a(n-1)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(b(n)=b(n-1)-4\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(c(n)=5 \\cdot c(n-1)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(d(n)=d(n-1)+n-1\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>For questions 6 – 8, match each sequence with one of the recursive definitions. Note that only the part of the definition showing the relationship between the current term and the previous term is given so as not to give away the solutions.</para>
      <para>3, 15, 75, 375</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(c(n)=5 \cdot c(n-1)\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.17.2 – 4.17.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q7-->
  <exercise data-content-id="de90b110-dd9b-4dab-a220-43138f2ab7ac" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(a(n)=\frac{1}{3}\cdot a(n-1)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(a(n)=\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot a(n-1)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(b(n)=b(n-1)-4\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(c(n)=5 \\cdot c(n-1)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(d(n)=d(n-1)+n-1\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>18, 6, 2, \(\frac{2}{3}\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(a(n)=\frac{1}{3}a(n-1)\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.17.2 – 4.17.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q9-->
  <exercise data-content-id="cbd7a717-07d5-4ad6-a639-e457a6d9956c" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(b(n)=b(n-1)-4\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(a(n)=\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot a(n-1)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(b(n)=b(n-1)-4\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(c(n)=5 \\cdot c(n-1)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(d(n)=d(n-1)+n-1\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>17, 13, 9, 5</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(b(n)=b(n-1)-4\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.17.2-–.16.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q10-->
  <exercise data-content-id="70384a16-aac0-49c2-a57c-91d05f23be77" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(k(1)=12, k(n)=k(n-1)-6\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(k(1)=12, k(n)=k(n)-6\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(k(1)=12, k(n)=k(n-1)-6\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(k(1)=12, k(n)=k(n-1)+6\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(k(1)=12, 6⋅k(n)=k(n-1)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> An arithmetic sequence \(k\) starts 12, 6, . . . and is represented by the graph below. </para>
      <para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/b9796b5a8c6fd4e1dbe3f5a42c3f01ad31965ef5"/></media></figure></para>
        <para>Which of the following is a recursive definition for sequence \(k\) when \(n\geq2\)?</para>
     
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(k(1)=12, k(n)=k(n-1)-6\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.17.2 – 4.17.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below this line-->
  <solution> </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> </div>
</div></section>
